                            <comment id="15349669" author="githubbot" created="Sat, 25 Jun 2016 14:36:01 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Github user prabhjyotsingh commented on the issue:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/1060&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/1060&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    Going back i.e. `history.back()`wouldn&apos;t for if someone has shared a link (for example) over chat/email  on which you don&apos;t have access to. Hence, I would recommend  `window.location.replace(&apos;/&apos;)` or anything that can take you to home page.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15349733" author="githubbot" created="Sat, 25 Jun 2016 17:32:28 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Github user AhyoungRyu commented on the issue:&lt;/p&gt;

