                            <comment id="15829971" author="kekchoze" created="Thu, 19 Jan 2017 13:54:48 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Would it be possible to change this so that:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;if a user who tries to access a notebook that they don&apos;t have access to, or&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;if they try to run a paragraph (or change the value of a dynamic field) without sufficient privileges&lt;br/&gt;
they would stay on the same page (or reload the page, or go back to the previous page they were on)?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;From a user experience POV, it could be frustrating to always be redirected to the home screen in the situations above.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
